        as a quotient of a polynomial ring
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the rational univariate
        representation of I or the rational univariate representation of S

Description
===========

This computes the rational univariate representation of a zero-dimensional
ideal in a polynomial ring.

+-----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y]                               |
|                                               |
|o1 = R                                         |
|                                               |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                            |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x*y - 1,2*x - y + 3)            |
|                                               |
|o2 = ideal (x*y - 1, 2x - y + 3)               |
|                                               |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : rationalUnivariateRepresentation(I)       |
|                                               |
|              2   3        - 3Z + 15  6Z + 21  |
|o3 = (x + y, Z  - -Z - 9, {---------, -------})|
|                  2          4Z - 3    4Z - 3  |
|                                               |
|o3 : Sequence                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i4 : rationalUnivariateRepresentation(R/I)     |
|                                               |
|              2   3        - 3Z + 15  6Z + 21  |
|o4 = (x + y, Z  - -Z - 9, {---------, -------})|
|                  2          4Z - 3    4Z - 3  |
|                                               |
|o4 : Sequence                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------+

