traceCount -- the degree of the reduced scheme of an Artinian ring
******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        traceCount(S)
        traceCount(f)
        traceCount(I)
        traceCount(l)
  * Inputs:
      * S, a *note quotient ring: (Macaulay2Doc)QuotientRing,, an Artinian ring
        over any field
      * f, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a univariate
        polynomial
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, a zero-dimensional ideal in a
        polynomial ring
      * l, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a system of polynomials with a
        finite number of solutions
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the degree of the reduced scheme
        of an Artinian ring

Description
===========

This computes the degree of the reduced scheme of an Artinian ring S over any
field, which is the number of distinct points of Spec S, after a base change to
an algebraically-closed field.

This counts the number of roots of a univariate polynomial f.

+------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y]                    |
|                                    |
|o1 = R                              |
|                                    |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                 |
+------------------------------------+
|i2 : f = (x^2 + 1)*(x + 1)*(x - 2)^2|
|                                    |
|      5     4    3    2             |
|o2 = x  - 3x  + x  + x  + 4         |
|                                    |
|o2 : R                              |
+------------------------------------+
|i3 : traceCount(f)                  |
|                                    |
|o3 = 4                              |
+------------------------------------+

If I is a zero-dimensional ideal of a polynomial ring, this computes the number
of distinct points of Spec (ring I)/I.

+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : I = ideal(5 - 3*x^2 - 3*y^2 + x^2*y^2, 1 + 2*x*y - 4*x*y^2 + 3*x^2*y)|
|                                                                          |
|             2 2     2     2        2        2                            |
|o4 = ideal (x y  - 3x  - 3y  + 5, 3x y - 4x*y  + 2x*y + 1)                |
|                                                                          |
|o4 : Ideal of R                                                           |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : traceCount(I)                                                        |
|                                                                          |
|o5 = 8                                                                    |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+

If l is a system of rational polynomials, then this computes the number of
distinct solutions.

+------------------------------------------+
|i6 : l = {y^2 - x^2 - 1,x - y^2 + 4*y - 2}|
|                                          |
|         2    2         2                 |
|o6 = {- x  + y  - 1, - y  + x + 4y - 2}   |
|                                          |
|o6 : List                                 |
+------------------------------------------+
|i7 : traceCount(l)                        |
|                                          |
|o7 = 4                                    |
+------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note traceForm: traceForm, -- the trace symmetric form of a polynomial in
    an Artinian ring
  * *note realCount: realCount, -- the number of real points of the spectrum of
    an Artinian ring (of characteristic 0)

Ways to use traceCount:
=======================

  * "traceCount(Ideal)"
  * "traceCount(List)"
  * "traceCount(QuotientRing)"
  * "traceCount(RingElement)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note traceCount: traceCount, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

